  "body": "The provider Test control in PR #3798 uses one message for all cloud request failures.\nA rejected key, a wrong model, missing credit, and a network error give the same status.\nThe reporter requested a key rejected status on #3781.\n\nClassify provider authentication failures without displaying the provider response or key.\nShow a key rejected status when authentication fails.\nKeep other request failures distinct from an authentication failure.\nAdd a deterministic pin for the authentication result and the safe displayed status.\nThe live-ai follow-up must also check the result with a wrong key.\n\nDone means: each cloud provider shows key rejected for an authentication failure, and tests pin this behavior.\n\neffort:medium - The change follows the existing provider status pattern.\n\nRefs #3781. Found in the review of #3798.\n",
